{{Short description|Second and final stage of the 2002 FIFA World Cup}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=February 2020}}
At the [[2002 FIFA World Cup]], the [[Single-elimination tournament|knockout stage]] was the second and final stage of the tournament, following the group stage. The top two teams from each group (16 in total) advanced to the knockout stage to compete in a single-elimination tournament. A match for third place was also played between the two losing semi-finalists.<ref>{{cite web |last=Manaschev |first=Erlan |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/2002full.html |title=World Cup 2002 – Match Details |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |date=3 July 2008 |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref>

<small>Note: Match kickoff times are given in local (South Korea and Japan) time; this is [[Time in South Korea|KST]] and [[Japan Standard Time|JST]] (UTC+9) during summer time.</small>

==Qualified teams==
The top two placed teams from each of the eight groups qualified for the knockout stage.

