===Denmark vs England===
After five minutes, [[David Beckham]] launched a corner towards [[Rio Ferdinand]], whose header was fumbled by [[Thomas Sørensen]] into the net.<ref name="news.bbc.co.uk">{{Cite web|url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport3/worldcup2002/hi/matches_wallchart/denmark_v_england/default.stm|title = BBC SPORT &#124; WORLD CUP &#124; Denmark v England &#124; England brush Danes aside}}</ref> [[Michael Owen]] doubled England's advantage after [[Trevor Sinclair]]'s pass was flicked to him by [[Nicky Butt]].<ref name="news.bbc.co.uk"/> England made it 3-0 one minute before half-time when a throw-in by [[Danny Mills]] was missed by [[Niclas Jensen]], with Beckham passing to [[Emile Heskey]] who swept the ball home.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2002/jun/16/worldcupfootball2002.sport13|title = Denmark 0 - 3 England|date = 16 June 2002}}</ref> In the second half, England appeared to take their foot off the pedal, possibly with a view to conserving energy for the next round: but were easily able to snuff out any rare Danish attacks, neither side coming particularly close to scoring again.
