===Mexico vs United States===
{{see also|Mexico–United States soccer rivalry}}
After eight minutes, [[Claudio Reyna]] managed to run through the right-hand side before sending the ball to [[Josh Wolff]], who then switched the ball over to [[Brian McBride]] who struck the ball into the net.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport3/worldcup2002/hi/matches_wallchart/mexico_v_usa/default.stm|title = BBC SPORT &#124; WORLD CUP &#124; Mexico v USA &#124; USA see off sorry Mexico}}</ref> [[Landon Donovan]] doubled the United States' advantage midway through the second half after [[Eddie Lewis (American soccer)|Eddie Lewis]] ran through the left-hand side before sending the ball towards Donovan who headed the ball home.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2002/jun/17/minutebyminute.worldcupfootball20021|title = Mexico 0 - 2 USA|date = 17 June 2002}}</ref> A frustrated Mexico also saw captain [[Rafael Márquez]] sent off late on by referee [[Vítor Melo Pereira]] for a dangerous tackle on [[Cobi Jones]].
